  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the window_cleaner experiencing futile effort",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the window_cleaner, who is depicted performing an absurdly excessive number of wipes (700 times) without achieving a clean result. The text 'when you wipe 700 times and there is still shit' directly addresses the viewer, implying that the user is the one who has experienced this frustrating situation. The rhetorical question 'i have a question. for god. why?' further reinforces this projection by inviting the user to identify with the character's exasperation. The user is thus projected onto the window_cleaner as the embodiment of the futility of effort described in the text.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
